[#4471](/kb/incidents/4471) is marked known: one issue, one fix queued. Read report by report, it holds
more than one problem. They share subject lines, so [decision 0001](/kb/decisions/0001-dedupe-by-subject)
merged them, but they have different causes and need different fixes. The parser fix that is queued
will not close all of them.

<Callout kind="warn">
Each problem below now has a ticket of its own. Count a report once, under its problem, not under #4471.
</Callout>

## The problems in #4471

<ProblemTable ticket={4471} issues={{ parser: 'https://github.com/aXenDeveloper/s01e03-what-it-shows/issues/1', hint: 'https://github.com/aXenDeveloper/s01e03-what-it-shows/issues/2', 'one-day': 'https://github.com/aXenDeveloper/s01e03-what-it-shows/issues/3' }} />

## How each one is told apart

**`parser`**: the shared parser reads every date month first. Every tenant on file writes the day
first, so day and month swap. It comes in through every channel. *"Booked for 2 July. The invite says
7 February."*

**`hint`**: tenants on `booking-v3` show `MM/DD/YYYY` under the date field. People type what the hint
says, and the form then reads the date the tenant's way, day first. It only comes in through the
booking form, and only from `booking-v3` tenants. The swap looks the same as `parser`, so subject and
body cannot tell them apart: the tenant's form and the channel can. Fixing the parser does not fix the
hint.

**`one-day`**: the date moves by one day, not by a swap. *"Client in Lisbon got Tuesday. Client in
Toronto got Monday. Same meeting."* *"Every booking in June is one day off. Only June."* The desk
already read these reports as a one-day move (`desk-notes.json`), but filed them under `parser` by
tenant. A one-day move between time zones is a different bug from a day/month swap, so it gets its own
ticket.

## Why one ticket hid them

- Decision 0001 merges on subject alone. *"Booking on the wrong date"* is the same subject for a
  `parser` report and a `hint` report.
- Intake tags a report from the reporter's browser, not from the tenant. The tag is a guess, and it
  disagrees with the problem often (see the table).
- The export repeats reports where its pages overlap. Count unique ids only.

## What the desk does now

1. New date reports: place them with `#lib/kb/problems` (tenant, form, channel), not by subject.
2. Merge into the problem's own ticket, not into #4471.
3. A report that reads as a one-day move goes to `one-day`, whatever its tenant.

